 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "orders lists [fruit, quantity, timestamp] string triples (quantity and timestamp are decimal integer strings). prices lists [fruit, unitPrice] pairs (unitPrice an integer, one pair per fruit). tiers lists [minQuantity, discountPercent] pairs with strictly increasing minQuantity. For each fruit, sort its orders by timestamp; consecutive orders whose timestamps differ by at most 600000 belong to the same purchase group (chaining). A group with Q total units costs Q * unitPrice, reduced by the discount of the tier with the largest minQuantity <= Q when the group has at least two orders (no discount for single orders or when no tier applies): cost = floor(Q * unitPrice * (100 - discountPercent) / 100). Return the total cost of all groups.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
